        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-19T12:44:17Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(geometry): bridge a fill hole to a walk vertex before a ray hit\n\nThe area preview of a 2D Adaptive with Containment Outside on the\nbiggest fig8 patch had no fill after #2760 made the fig8 mesh finer.\nThe hole of that region looks onto a steep, short outer edge. The\ncomputed ray hit on that edge rounds to a point 3e-16 inside the\nmaterial, so the ear clipper saw it strictly inside the ears beside it\nand stopped with \"no ear in a non-triangle walk\". A smaller region with\nthe same edge lost a part of its fill with no error.\n\nmerge_hole now tries the walk vertices first, nearest first, and keeps\nthe ray hits as the last resort. The candidate checks do not change.\nThe fill is display-only.\n\nFixes #2762\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
